  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed both as a noun and as a する verb ({酷使|こくし}する). Common objects of {酷使|こくし} include {体|からだ} (body), {目|め} (eyes), {声帯|せいたい} (vocal cords), and machinery. Always has a negative connotation.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {体|からだ}を{酷使|こくし}する (to overwork one's body)\n- {目|め}を{酷使|こくし}する (to strain one's eyes)\n- {労働者|ろうどうしゃ}を{酷使|こくし}する (to overwork laborers)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {使|つか}い{過|す}ぎ: overuse — milder and more neutral than {酷使|こくし}, which implies cruelty or mercilessness",
